syntax: zsh case pattern groups may hold empty alternatives

A parenthesized group in a zsh pattern may have an empty alternative, which
matches the empty string, so zsh -n accepts, and zsh matches,

	case $cmd in
	  (|l)server) ;;            # server or lserver
	  (un|)install|freeze) ;;   # install, uninstall or freeze
	  (kvm-|)buildid-list) ;;
	esac

zsh's own completion functions use the form in many case items. The parser
read every alternative of a group as a pattern word and failed on the empty
one with "case patterns must consist of words".

With LangZsh, an alternative of a group that is part of a pattern may now be
empty. The optional "(" before the patterns of a case item, as in
`(a|b) cmd`, still needs a word for every pattern.

Reproducer, before this change: `case i in (|l)s) ;; esac` with LangZsh
failed with "case patterns must consist of words".

